course: dictionary
lesson: 12240
title: Words of comfort
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A consolation is comfort given to someone who is sad or disappointed. When a friend sits with you after you lose a game, they are offering consolation. The word is a noun, and when you mean comfort in general it has no plural.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Mia lost the spelling bee, but her mum gave her a big hug and a warm drink.» The hug and the drink are there to make Mia feel better, so consolation must mean comfort. Swap the meaning in: "her mum gave her a big hug and comfort" still makes sense.
explain: Consolation can also mean a thing or person that makes a bad situation a little better. «It's some consolation that the rain stopped before the picnic.» The rain was still a problem, but the good news helps. Words like "some" and "at least" often show consolation.
explain: In sport, consolation has special uses. A consolation prize is a small prize for someone who did not win. A consolation goal is scored by a team that is losing badly, so it does not change the result, but it gives the team something to cheer about.
fact: Consolation means comfort given to someone who is sad or disappointed.
fact: Consolation can also mean a person or thing that makes a bad situation a little easier.
fact: A «consolation prize» is a small prize for someone who did not win.
fact: A «consolation goal» is scored by a team that is losing badly.
fact: You can say «It's some consolation that...» to mean something good helps a little with something bad.
exercise: «After the team lost the final, the coach offered consolation to the sad players.» What does consolation mean here? | *Comfort for people who are sad | A long holiday | A new kit for next season | A fine for playing badly
exercise: «It's some consolation that the rain stopped before the picnic.» What does consolation suggest? | A rude word for rain | A type of cloud | A kind of picnic food | *Something good that makes a bad thing a little better
exercise: «She didn't win the race, but she got a consolation prize for her hard work.» What is a consolation prize? | The biggest prize of all | *A small prize for someone who did not win | A prize given only to the coach
test: «Ben's team was losing 5-0, but in the last minute he scored a consolation goal.» Why is the goal called a consolation? | It was scored by the other team | *It gave his losing team something good to cheer about | It was an own goal | The goal made his team win the match
test: Which sentence uses consolation to mean comfort for someone who is sad? | The bus stop is near the consolation shop. | *Her friends' kind words were a real consolation after the loss. | The shop sells consolation cards for every birthday.
exam: What does it mean when someone says «It's some consolation that we still have the cake»? | The cake is very expensive | Nobody likes cake | *Something good that makes a bad thing a little easier | We must share the cake with everyone
